# Magic: the same spells cast twice, the physics of spells and bodies off (OpenGothic's canned throw, the target
# never leaves the ground in a whirlwind, a fireball leaves it standing) and on (the spell's push on the body by
# its mass, ragdoll); each `rec` is a beat of the short, the two takes stacked (shorts/compare/film.sh, cut.py).
# `off:` lines run in the "off" take only. Daylight, no AI server. The `spell fixture` scenes stand on open ground
# by Xardas' tower the bench picks: a farmer 7 m before the hero, a bandit beside him, a body and a lute, a pan
# and a mace on the ground (the wind fixture: a troll instead of the body and the things).
seed 73013
cheat god
set time 12 0
overlay off
view full
off: spell feature off
off: ragdoll off
off: living off

# fireball: the farmer, the body and the things by him
spell fixture fire
spell equip 23
wait 1200
cam follow 420 140 70
cam look 80
wait 600
rec fireball
cam hold
spell cast 600
wait 4500
stop

# whirlwind: lifts the farmer
spell fixture field
spell equip 71
wait 1200
cam follow 600 120 60
cam look 300
wait 600
rec whirlwind
cam hold
spell cast 600
wait 8000
stop

# troll: the wind fist at a troll; it weighs 600 kg
spell fixture wind
spell target troll
spell equip 26
wait 1200
cam follow 850 230 45
cam look 170
wait 600
rec troll
cam hold
spell cast 600
wait 4000
stop
spell clear
